  "summary": "A citizen group, DeFlock Everett, is gathering signatures for two ballot initiatives \u2014 one to ban the city's use of Flock ALPR cameras and require deletion of collected data, and another to restrict police drone use. The article notes Everett paused and reactivated its Flock network in 2026 and that neighboring Lynnwood, Mountlake Terrace, and Edmonds have canceled their Flock contracts amid concerns over federal immigration access.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Since December 2025, Lynnwood , Mountlake Terrace and Edmonds have canceled their contracts with Flock Safety following reports of federal immigration enforcement accessing local networks .",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "The first initiative would prohibit the city from using Flock Safety cameras or any other \"similar ALPR surveillance system.\"",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "In February, Everett paused its network after a Snohomish County judge ruled that the footage would be subject to public records requests. The city reactivated its network in April following a new state law that explicitly exempts the footage from the Public Records Act.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    }
  ],
